WEBVTT

00:00:00.013 --> 00:00:03.997
Partitions are one of the basic units of Spark parallelism.

00:00:03.997 --> 00:00:07.817
Imagine a very large book divided into sections.

00:00:07.817 --> 00:00:11.902
Different workers can read different sections at the same time.

00:00:11.902 --> 00:00:18.255
In Spark, partitions give executors pieces of the dataset that can be processed in parallel.

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:24.381
If there are too few partitions, we may not use the available workers effectively.

00:00:24.381 --> 00:00:31.641
If there are far too many tiny partitions, Spark spends more time coordinating small tasks.

00:00:31.641 --> 00:00:36.836
At this stage, you do not need to tune partition counts perfectly.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:42.498
I want you to understand why partitioning affects both parallelism and overhead.
